 SMLC & SKV Universal QR Tracking SystemArchitected by: DJ Werewolf (Kevin Frutiger)Powered by: Support My Local Community (SMLC)📌 Project OverviewThis repository manages a high-intelligence, "Universal" QR code system for S&K Venture Signs and Support My Local Community.Unlike traditional static QR codes, this system uses Dynamic Geolocation Redirects. This allows a single printed QR code to work nationwide while providing granular, location-specific tracking data (State, City, and Zip Code) directly in Google Analytics.🧠 How the "Smart Redirect" WorksEvery Universal QR code in this system points to a dedicated staging page on the SMLC platform. When a user scans the code, the following process occurs in under one second:The Entry: The user's device hits the staging URL (e.g., /universal-smlc-trailer/).The Geo-Ping: A lightweight JavaScript function pings an IP-based geolocation API to identify the user's current State, City, and Zip Code.The Tagging: The system builds a custom UTM Campaign Tag based on that location (e.g., il_flora_62839_smlc_trailer).The Hand-off: The user is instantly redirected to the final destination (SKV or SMLC homepage) with the tracking tags attached.🗺️ Master Redirect DirectoryCategoryStaging URL (The "Brain")Final DestinationS&K Universal Trailer/go-reroute/skventuresigns.comS&K Stationary Billboard/go-billboard-stationary/skventuresigns.comS&K Universal Social/universal-social-skv/skventuresigns.comSMLC Universal Trailer/universal-smlc-trailer/supportmylocalcommunity.comSMLC Stationary Billboard/universal-stationary-billboard/supportmylocalcommunity.comSMLC Universal Social/universal-social-smlc/supportmylocalcommunity.com✨ Key Features & BenefitsZero-Touch Maintenance: Print the QR code once. If the trailer moves from Illinois to Indiana, the tracking updates automatically without changing the sign.Granular Analytics: Capture specific Zip Code data to see exactly which intersections or neighborhoods are driving the most engagement.Consolidated Branding: All traffic is sourced through supportmylocalcommunity, providing clear proof of value for the SMLC platform as a marketing engine.Infrastructure-Free: No complex backend or database required; the logic is handled entirely by client-side JavaScript and IP-geolocation.🛠️ Automation & WorkflowThe images in the /qrcode folder are generated and synced via a custom Google Apps Script integrated with the "SMLC UTM Source Tracking" spreadsheet.Spreadsheet: URL parameters are managed in Google Sheets.Automation: The script generates high-resolution .png files.Sync: Files are pushed directly to this GitHub repository for deployment.Technical NoteThis system utilizes IP-based geolocation (Tower-based) to ensure a "Frictionless" user experience. No GPS permissions are required from the user, ensuring a 100% success rate for redirects.How to Use this README:Go to your GitHub repository.Click Add file > Create new file.Name it README.md.Paste the content above and click Commit changes.Now, whenever Scott (or anyone else) opens the repo, they’ll see this professional dashboard explaining exactly what you've built. Does this cover everything you wanted to explain to him?
